  "notes": "ETYMOLOGY:\n{無|む} (without) + {闇|やみ} (darkness) → acting blindly, without seeing\n\nVARIATIONS:\n- {無闇|むやみ}: attributive form\n- {無闇|むやみ}やたらに: emphatically reckless\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {無闇|むやみ}に{手|て}を{出|だ}す: to meddle carelessly\n- {無闇|むやみ}に{信|しん}じる: to believe blindly\n- {無闇|むやみ}に{動|うご}く: to move around recklessly\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- やたらに: randomly, excessively\n- {軽率|けいそつ}に: rashly, thoughtlessly\n- みだりに: indiscriminately",
